\section{Error analysis}
\label{app:errors}

A held-out AUROC reports how often a direction ranks a positive above a negative. It says nothing
about \emph{which} items it gets wrong, and two pipelines with identical AUROC are different
objects if one errs at random and the other errs on an identifiable subgroup. We therefore
recompute per-item predictions from the cached activations, using the same split and seed as the
experiment, and decide each item by thresholding at the midpoint of the two class means---a rule
the direction itself implies rather than one tuned on the test set.

